## 2026-08-29 - US-006: Preserve progress file when resuming a partial run

Completed. `runWavesIsolated` in src/orchestrator.ts always called
`generateProgress` and overwrote `progress.md` with a fresh,
all-unchecked object, so resuming after a partial run (e.g. after a
crash or a manual re-invocation) discarded the record of tickets
that had already completed in the prior run.

Change: added two exports to src/progress.ts:
- `readProgress(progressPath)`: parses an existing progress.md
  (the format produced by `renderProgress`) back into a
  `ProgressData` object, or returns `null` if the file does not
  exist. Ticket identity is keyed by filename (parsed with a local
  `TICKET_FILENAME_RE`, not imported from orchestrator.ts, to avoid
  a circular module dependency between progress.ts and
  orchestrator.ts).
- `mergeProgress(fresh, existing)`: given a freshly generated
  `ProgressData` and an `existing` one (or `null`), returns a new
  `ProgressData` whose tickets are the fresh set, except tickets
  that were `done: true` in `existing` are replaced wholesale with
  the existing (completed) record, carrying forward `branch`,
  `exitCode`, and `completedAt`. Returns `fresh` unchanged when
  `existing` is `null`.

`runWavesIsolated` now calls
`mergeProgress(generateProgress(...), readProgress(progressPath))`
before the initial `writeProgress`, so a pre-existing progress.md's
completed tickets survive a resumed run; when no file exists yet,
behavior is unchanged (identical to calling `generateProgress` alone).

