across 5 rounds of 10...") to test/worktree.test.ts: for 5 rounds,
fires 10 concurrent createWorktree calls (distinct ticket nums per
call, so distinct paths/branches) via Promise.all and asserts every
resulting worktree path exists.

Gotcha: I could not get this to fail pre-fix, even at full 50-way
concurrency in one Promise.all batch against a real temp repo
(tested standalone via a throwaway script, not just the 5x10
harness) -- this machine's git version handles concurrent
`worktree add` on distinct branches/paths without corruption,
likely via its own internal ref-lock retries. The PRD's concern
(races on shared refs) is plausible on other environments -- slower
filesystems, NFS-backed repos, or older git versions with weaker
locking -- so implemented serialization as specified rather than
skipping it. The added test is a regression guard for the
serialized behavior, not a demonstrated repro of the original race.

