run settles (`finish()` and the `proc.on('error', ...)` handler).
Exported `killRunningAgents()` iterates the set and calls
`killProcessGroup` on each pid -- it does not clear the set itself;
that happens naturally as each killed process's `finish()`/`error`
handler fires.

`src/index.ts` now installs `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM` handlers right after
`createDisplay()` in `runExecute`, before the run starts. Both call
a shared `onSignal(exitCode)` that calls `killRunningAgents()`,
`display.cleanup()`, then `process.exit()` with 130 (SIGINT) or 143
(SIGTERM). These are only installed once per CLI invocation, so
there's no listener-accumulation concern.

Tests: `test/display.test.ts` gained two tests asserting
`process.listenerCount('SIGINT'|'SIGTERM')` is unchanged across
`startWave` and `cleanup`. `test/integration.test.ts` gained a unit
test spawning a hanging agent (`mock-agent-hang.js`) via
`spawnAgent`, calling `killRunningAgents()`, and asserting the
promise resolves promptly with a nonzero exit code and
`timedOut:false` (to distinguish the kill path from the timeout
path); a no-op test for an empty registry; and a full CLI subprocess
test that spawns the built CLI with `mock-agent-grandchild-hang.js`
as the provider, waits for the agent's grandchild pid file to
appear, sends `SIGINT` to the CLI process, and asserts both that the
CLI exits 130 and that the grandchild process is actually dead (not
just orphaned).

Confirmed red first: with the orchestrator/display changes in place
but the `src/index.ts` signal-handler wiring temporarily removed,
the CLI-subprocess test failed both assertions. `not ok 137 CLI
exits 130 on SIGINT` (expected 130, actual -1) -- with no installed
handler, Node terminates the process via the signal itself rather
than calling `process.exit(130)`, so the `exit` event fires with
`code:null`. `not ok 138 the agent's child process was killed too`
(expected false, actual true) -- nothing sent a signal to the
agent's process group, so the grandchild was still alive after the
CLI died. Re-adding the handler wiring in `src/index.ts` turned both
green.

Verified via `npm run build` (typecheck), `npm run lint`, the
targeted `test/display.test.ts` and `test/integration.test.ts`
bundles, and the full suite.

All 674 tests pass (setup: 79, orchestrator: 156, worktree: 75,
progress: 57, merge: 40, display: 86, testcmd: 13, integration: 168).
Lint clean.

