## 2026-09-03 - US-008: A throw inside an attempt fails that attempt, not the wave

Completed. `runTicketAttempt` in src/orchestrator.ts could throw
when a ticket's worktree is destroyed mid-run (e.g. by the agent
deleting its own cwd). The `isDirty` / `hasNewCommits` calls use
`execFileSync` which throws ENOENT when the directory no longer
exists, and since `runTicketAttempts` had no try/catch around its
`runTicketAttempt` call, the rejection propagated through
`Promise.all` in `runWavesIsolated` and crashed the entire wave.

Changes:
1. Added `'error'` kind to the `TicketOutcome` discriminated union
   (src/orchestrator.ts:1127) with an `error:unknown` field.
2. Wrapped the `runTicketAttempt` call in `runTicketAttempts` with
   try/catch (src/orchestrator.ts:1304-1311). A caught error returns
   `{ kind:'error', error }` immediately -- no retry, since the
   error is structural (missing directory), not a transient agent
   failure.
3. Added `'error'` handling in `runWavesIsolated`'s outcome loop
   (src/orchestrator.ts:1649-1657): adds the ticket to `failedNums`,
   sets display status to `'failed'`, logs the error, and continues
   to the next ticket.

Created test/mock-agent-delete-worktree-01.js: for ticket 01-*,
deletes its own cwd (the worktree directory) then exits 0. For
all other tickets, behaves like mock-agent-pass.js.

Added 1 new integration test to test/integration.test.ts: two
independent tickets in one wave, ticket 01 uses the
delete-worktree mock. Asserts ticket 01 stays ready-for-agent
(error failed the ticket), ticket 02 reaches done (wave survived),
and result.allDone is false.

