## 2026-09-04 - US-003: Kill process group on grace timeout

Completed. In `spawnAgent` (src/orchestrator.ts), the grace timer
callback that fires when the agent exits but a grandchild holds
the stdout pipe open previously only destroyed the streams and
resolved the promise. Now it calls `killProcessGroup(proc.pid)`
before destroying streams, so dev servers and watchers spawned by
the agent do not survive indefinitely.

Created test/mock-agent-grandchild-exit.js: spawns a long-lived
grandchild sharing stdout via `stdio:['ignore', 'inherit',
'inherit']`, writes the grandchild pid to `./grandchild.pid`,
then calls `process.exit(0)`. Unlike the existing
mock-agent-grandchild-hang.js (which never exits and exercises
the timeout path), this mock exercises the grace timer path where
the agent exits voluntarily but the grandchild keeps the pipe.

Added 1 new test to test/integration.test.ts: verifies spawnAgent
resolves within 10s, exitCode is 0, timedOut is false, and the
grandchild process is no longer alive after the grace timer fires.

Gotcha: SIGKILL is delivered immediately but the grandchild
becomes a zombie until init reaps it. `process.kill(pid, 0)`
returns success for zombies, so the test needs a short delay
(200ms) between spawnAgent resolving and the alive check to avoid
a false positive.

All 710 tests pass (setup: 87, orchestrator: 168, worktree: 77,
progress: 57, merge: 40, display: 86, testcmd: 13,
integration: 182).
